4. Write a example of basic grid structure in Bootstrap?

Ans. Bootstrap uses a12-column grid system  to create responsive layouts. A basic grid structure contains a container, a row, and columns.

Example:

<div class="container">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-4">Column 1</div>
        <div class="col-4">Column 2</div>
        <div class="col-4">Column 3</div>
    </div>
</div>
 

Here, the row is divided into three equal columns. Each  col-4  takes 4 out of the 12 available columns, so together they occupy the complete row.

5. What is   Selectors?

Ans.   selectors are used to select HTML elements  that we want to style. They tell the browser which elements a particular   rule should be applied to.

For example:

p {
    color: blue;
}
 
Here,  p  is an element selector, so the style will be applied to all paragraph elements.

Some common types of selectors are:

 Element selector: p
 Class selector: .box
 ID selector: #heading
 Universal selector: *
 Group selector: h1, p

Selectors make it easier to apply specific styles to different elements on a webpage.

